  "name": "Question 3",
  "problem": "Simplify the trigonometric expression $\\frac{{cos}^{4}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }.$",
  "worked_solution": "First, we factor the numerator:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{4}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }=\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta ({cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta )+{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }\n$$\n\nNext, we use the Pythagorean identity to rewrite the expression in the parentheses, and then we simplify the resulting expression as much as possible:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta ({cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta )+{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } & =\\frac{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot 1+{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot {cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\cdot \\cancel{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }}{\\cancel{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }\\cdot \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta } \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta \\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{{cos}^{4}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta {sin}^{2}\u2061\\theta +{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta }{{cos}^{2}\u2061\\theta \\operatorname{sin}\u2061\\theta }=2\\operatorname{csc}\u2061\\theta .\n$$",
